From 0fdf7fd411a54b8c026d4aa5286d5ca5f8d4c28b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:04:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] microblaze: keep local labels out of the symbol table

Fixup for "gas: microblaze: emit ADD and SUB for code label
differences" (the SUB half in md_apply_fix) and "gas: microblaze: emit
CFA advances as relocations" (the SUB and SUB6 half in
microblaze_cfa_fix); "emit line advances as relocations" inherits it
through the first.

md_apply_fix and microblaze_cfa_fix make the SUB half of an ADD/SUB
pair when fixup_segment applies the fixup, after adjust_reloc_syms has
replaced local symbols with section symbols.  The ADD half names
.text+offset, but the SUB half names the label itself, so every such
label is written to the symbol table.  An object assembled with -g
lists five "L0^A" symbols (gas's fake label) for a three-instruction
function with CFI, and a gcc -g -O2 program linked with --relax keeps
73 $L* and 11 L0^A symbols, which objdump -d then uses to name code
("00000458 <$LCFI5>:").

Make the SUB half against the section symbol plus an offset too, with
the same conditions as adjust_reloc_syms.  ld already corrects the
addend of an ADD or SUB relocation against a section symbol when
relaxation deletes code before it ("microblaze: adjust ADD and SUB
relocations when relaxing").  A gcc -g -O2 program linked with --relax
now has the same .debug_info, .debug_line and .eh_frame contents as
before, and no local labels from its own objects.

readelf subtracted the addend of a SUB relocation with the wrong sign,
computing field + A - S rather than field - (S + A).  No SUB
relocation had an addend before, but now the line table of DWARF2 13
ended at 0x58 instead of 0x18.  Subtract the addend.  This applies to
the RISC-V and LoongArch SUB relocations too, which gas emits against
labels with no addend.

Objects from an older assembler still carry such labels.  As RISC-V
does (PR27584, PR27916), treat MicroBlaze local labels as target
special symbols, so that nm omits them, and do not choose them as
function names.

bfd/
	* elf32-microblaze.c (microblaze_elf_is_target_special_symbol)
	(microblaze_elf_maybe_function_sym): New functions.
	(bfd_elf32_bfd_is_target_special_symbol)
	(elf_backend_maybe_function_sym): Define.

binutils/
	* readelf.c (apply_relocations): Subtract the addend of a
	subtracting relocation.

gas/
	* config/tc-microblaze.c (microblaze_adjust_sub_sym): New function.
	(microblaze_cfa_fix, md_apply_fix): Use it for the SUB half.
	* testsuite/gas/microblaze/local-syms.d: New test.
	* testsuite/gas/microblaze/local-syms.exp: New file.
	* testsuite/gas/microblaze/local-syms.s: New file.
	* testsuite/gas/microblaze/dwarf2-fixed-advance.d: Expect the
	SUB16 relocations against .text.
	* testsuite/gas/microblaze/reloc_diff.d: Expect the SUB relocations
	against .text.
	* testsuite/gas/microblaze/reloc_diff_far.d: Likewise.
	* testsuite/gas/microblaze/reloc_diff_code.d: Likewise.

ld/
	* testsuite/ld-microblaze/local-syms.d: New test.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
